Keep the heartbeat's text in the binary

run-368's assembly shows why no round could ever find 'nio: HB ' in the object:
clang unrolled nio_dc_puts over the constant string and emitted one putc per
character with the character in an immediate (`mov w0, #110` for 'n'), so the
literal never materialises.  The kernel prints it -- the panel has said
'nio: HB 1 ...' all along -- but no byte search can see it.

Mark both writers noinline, so the string has to exist as data and the marker
checks (this series' guard, the round watcher) can tell a stale kernel from a
fresh one again.
